From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: zero the gen1 empty-buffer packets

iris_hfi_gen1_queue_input_buffer() builds the compressed (decoder) and
uncompressed (encoder) EMPTY_BUFFER packets on the stack and fills every
field except extradata_buffer and data. On a kernel built without
CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO the firmware receives stack contents there,
and extradata_buffer is a device address in HFI: a stale non-zero value
may make the firmware look for an extradata buffer the driver never
allocated. The FILL_BUFFER packet next to it already sets both fields to
0 explicitly.

Zero-initialise both packets, as the driver never attaches extradata to
an empty buffer. Kernels built with CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO already
send zeros, so for them nothing changes.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index b43d86c57..49911c91a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -310,8 +310,9 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_session_continue(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 
 static int iris_hfi_gen1_queue_input_buffer(struct iris_inst *inst, struct iris_buffer *buf)
 {
-	struct hfi_session_empty_buffer_compressed_pkt com_ip_pkt;
-	struct hfi_session_empty_buffer_uncompressed_pkt uncom_ip_pkt;
+	/* extradata_buffer and data are never set below: send zeros, not stack. */
+	struct hfi_session_empty_buffer_compressed_pkt com_ip_pkt = {};
+	struct hfi_session_empty_buffer_uncompressed_pkt uncom_ip_pkt = {};
 
 	if (inst->domain == DECODER) {
 		com_ip_pkt.shdr.hdr.size = sizeof(struct hfi_session_empty_buffer_compressed_pkt);
